    "description": {
      "value": "<p>Requires Attunement</p><p><a href=\"https://amellwind-mh-dn-d5e-foundry-toolbox-2.vercel.app/weapons?weapon=Heavy+Bowgun\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Open Heavy Bowgun in the Toolbox</a></p><p>Ammo DC = 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Dexterity modifier</p><hr><h3>Features</h3><div style=\"margin:0.65em 0;padding:0.55em 0.7em;border-left:3px solid #c0c0c0;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.04);border-radius:0 4px 4px 0\"><p><strong style=\"color:#c0c0c0\">Mastery (Slow)</strong></p><p>If you hit a creature with this weapon and deal damage to it, you can reduce its Speed by 10 feet until the start of your next turn. If the creature is hit more than once by weapons that have this property, the Speed reduction doesn't exceed 10 feet.</p></div><div style=\"margin:0.65em 0;padding:0.55em 0.7em;border-left:3px solid #ff8000;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.04);border-radius:0 4px 4px 0\"><p><strong style=\"color:#c0c0c0\">Magazine</strong></p><p>The weapon holds a maximum of 4 loaded rounds at a time. When the magazine reaches 0, you must reload it before you can fire again.</p><div style=\"margin:0.45em 0 0.1em 0.35em;padding:0.4em 0.55em;border-left:2px solid #1eff00;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border-radius:0 3px 3px 0\"><p>▸ Upgrade — <strong style=\"color:#1eff00\">Magazine Upgrade I</strong></p><p>Your magazine capacity increases to 6 rounds of standard ammunition (Normal, Pierce, or Spread).</p></div><div style=\"margin:0.45em 0 0.1em 0.35em;padding:0.4em 0.55em;border-left:2px solid #0070dd;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border-radius:0 3px 3px 0\"><p>▸ Upgrade — <strong style=\"color:#0070dd\">Magazine Upgrade II</strong></p><p>Your magazine capacity increases to 8 rounds of standard ammunition.</p></div><div style=\"margin:0.45em 0 0.1em 0.35em;padding:0.4em 0.55em;border-left:2px solid #a335ee;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border-radius:0 3px 3px 0\"><p>▸ Upgrade — <strong style=\"color:#a335ee\">Magazine Upgrade III</strong></p><p>Your magazine capacity increases to 10 rounds of standard ammunition.</p></div><div style=\"margin:0.45em 0 0.1em 0.35em;padding:0.4em 0.55em;border-left:2px solid #ff8000;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border-radius:0 3px 3px 0\"><p>▸ Upgrade — <strong style=\"color:#ff8000\">Magazine Upgrade IV</strong></p><p>Your magazine capacity increases to 12 rounds of standard ammunition.</p></div></div><div style=\"margin:0.65em 0;padding:0.55em 0.7em;border-left:3px solid #c0c0c0;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.04);border-radius:0 4px 4px 0\"><p><strong style=\"color:#c0c0c0\">Reload</strong></p><p><strong>Action.</strong></p><p>You can fully reload your magazine using an Action or a Bonus Action. When you do so, you choose the type of ammunition the weapon will contain.</p></div><div style=\"margin:0.65em 0;padding:0.55em 0.7em;border-left:3px solid #1eff00;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.04);border-radius:0 4px 4px 0\"><p><strong style=\"color:#1eff00\">Ignition</strong></p><p>Whenever you hit a creature with this weapon, you gain 1 Ignition (maximum 3). Ignition remains until you spend it and is not lost when the magazine is empty.</p></div><div style=\"margin:0.65em 0;padding:0.55em 0.7em;border-left:3px solid #a335ee;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.04);border-radius:0 4px 4px 0\"><p><strong style=\"color:#1eff00\">Wyvernheart</strong></p><p><strong>Bonus Action.</strong></p><p>Spend 1 Ignition to make one additional attack with this weapon as a Bonus Action. If you already hit a creature with this weapon this turn, this extra attack deals an extra [[/r 1d6]] Piercing damage.</p><div style=\"margin:0.45em 0 0.1em 0.35em;padding:0.4em 0.55em;border-left:2px solid #0070dd;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border-radius:0 3px 3px 0\"><p>▸ Upgrade — <strong style=\"color:#0070dd\">Wyvernheart Upgrade I</strong></p><p>When you use Wyvernheart after already hitting a creature with this weapon this turn, the extra damage increases to [[/r 1d8]] Piercing.</p></div><div style=\"margin:0.45em 0 0.1em 0.35em;padding:0.4em 0.55em;border-left:2px solid #a335ee;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border-radius:0 3px 3px 0\"><p>▸ Upgrade — <strong style=\"color:#a335ee\">Wyvernheart Upgrade II</strong></p><p>When you use Wyvernheart after already hitting a creature with this weapon this turn, the extra damage increases to [[/r 1d10]] Piercing.</p></div></div><div style=\"margin:0.65em 0;padding:0.55em 0.7em;border-left:3px solid #0070dd;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.04);border-radius:0 4px 4px 0\"><p><strong style=\"color:#1eff00\">Guard</strong></p><p><strong>Reaction.</strong></p><p>When a creature you can see hits you with an attack while you are wielding this weapon, you can use your Reaction to roll [[/r 1d4]] and add it to your AC against that attack, potentially causing it to miss. You cannot use Guard on the same turn you used Wyvernheart.</p><div style=\"margin:0.45em 0 0.1em 0.35em;padding:0.4em 0.55em;border-left:2px solid #0070dd;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border-radius:0 3px 3px 0\"><p>▸ Upgrade — <strong style=\"color:#0070dd\">Guard Upgrade I</strong></p><p>When you use Guard, you roll [[/r 1d6]] instead of [[/r 1d4]] and add it to your AC against the triggering attack.</p></div></div><div style=\"margin:0.65em 0;padding:0.55em 0.7em;border-left:3px solid #ff8000;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.04);border-radius:0 4px 4px 0\"><p><strong style=\"color:#1eff00\">Special Ammo</strong></p><p>Due to barrel pressure limits, you can load a maximum of 2 Special Ammo rounds into the magazine during a reload. Once these are expended, you must reload to switch back to another ammunition type.</p><div style=\"margin:0.45em 0 0.1em 0.35em;padding:0.4em 0.55em;border-left:2px solid #0070dd;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border-radius:0 3px 3px 0\"><p>▸ Upgrade — <strong style=\"color:#0070dd\">Special Ammo Upgrade I</strong></p><p>Your magazine can now hold up to 4 Special Ammo rounds.</p></div><div style=\"margin:0.45em 0 0.1em 0.35em;padding:0.4em 0.55em;border-left:2px solid #a335ee;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border-radius:0 3px 3px 0\"><p>▸ Upgrade — <strong style=\"color:#a335ee\">Special Ammo Upgrade II</strong></p><p>Your magazine can now hold up to 6 Special Ammo rounds.</p></div><div style=\"margin:0.45em 0 0.1em 0.35em;padding:0.4em 0.55em;border-left:2px solid #ff8000;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border-radius:0 3px 3px 0\"><p>▸ Upgrade — <strong style=\"color:#ff8000\">Special Ammo Upgrade III</strong></p><p>Your magazine can now hold up to 8 Special Ammo rounds.</p></div></div><div style=\"margin:0.65em 0;padding:0.55em 0.7em;border-left:3px solid #0070dd;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.04);border-radius:0 4px 4px 0\"><p><strong style=\"color:#0070dd\">Wyverncounter</strong></p><p>When you use Guard and the triggering attack misses you, you can spend 1 Ignition to make one attack with this weapon against that creature (no additional action required). This attack consumes 1 loaded round and does not apply a special ammunition effect. If the creature is within 15 feet of you, the attack deals an extra [[/r 1d8]] Piercing damage. You cannot use Wyverncounter on a turn you used Wyvernheart.</p></div><div style=\"margin:0.65em 0;padding:0.55em 0.7em;border-left:3px solid #ff8000;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.04);border-radius:0 4px 4px 0\"><p><strong style=\"color:#a335ee\">Wyvernpiercer</strong></p><p><strong>Action.</strong></p><p>As an Action, you can spend 2 Ignition and 1 loaded round to fire a focused shot in an 80-foot line that is 5 feet wide. This shot does not apply a special ammunition effect. Make a single attack roll and compare it against the AC of each creature in that line. A creature hit takes the weapon's normal damage plus [[/r 2d10]] Piercing damage. After you use Wyvernpiercer, you cannot use Guard until the start of your next turn.</p><div style=\"margin:0.45em 0 0.1em 0.35em;padding:0.4em 0.55em;border-left:2px solid #ff8000;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border-radius:0 3px 3px 0\"><p>▸ Upgrade — <strong style=\"color:#ff8000\">Wyvernpiercer Upgrade</strong></p><p>Your Wyvernpiercer line increases to 100 feet, and a creature hit takes the weapon's normal damage plus [[/r 4d10]] Piercing damage.</p></div></div><div style=\"margin:0.65em 0;padding:0.55em 0.7em;border-left:3px solid #ff8000;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.04);border-radius:0 4px 4px 0\"><p><strong style=\"color:#ff8000\">Ignition Mode</strong></p><p><strong>Bonus Action.</strong></p><p>As a Bonus Action, you can enter Ignition Mode for 1 minute. You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Proficiency Bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest. While Ignition Mode is active, you cannot use Guard or Wyverncounter; whenever you hit a creature with this weapon, you gain 2 Ignition instead of 1 (maximum still 3); and you can use Wyvernpiercer as a Bonus Action.</p></div><h3>Ammunition</h3><div style=\"margin:0.65em 0;padding:0.55em 0.7em;border-left:3px solid #a335ee;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.04);border-radius:0 4px 4px 0\"><p><strong style=\"color:#c0c0c0\">Normal Ammo</strong></p><p>Deals the weapon's base damage ([[/r 1d10]] Piercing) to a single target.</p><div style=\"margin:0.45em 0 0.1em 0.35em;padding:0.4em 0.55em;border-left:2px solid #a335ee;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border-radius:0 3px 3px 0\"><p>▸ Upgrade — <strong style=\"color:#a335ee\">Normal Ammo Upgrade</strong></p><p>Your Normal Ammo now deals an extra [[/r 1d6]] Piercing damage.</p></div></div><div style=\"margin:0.65em 0;padding:0.55em 0.7em;border-left:3px solid #a335ee;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.04);border-radius:0 4px 4px 0\"><p><strong style=\"color:#1eff00\">Pierce Ammo</strong></p><p>You fire in a 40-foot line that is 5 feet wide. Make a single attack roll and compare it against the AC of each creature in that line. All creatures hit take the weapon's normal damage.</p><div style=\"margin:0.45em 0 0.1em 0.35em;padding:0.4em 0.55em;border-left:2px solid #a335ee;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border-radius:0 3px 3px 0\"><p>▸ Upgrade — <strong style=\"color:#a335ee\">Pierce Ammo Upgrade</strong></p><p>Your Pierce Ammo now deals an extra [[/r 1d6]] Piercing damage.</p></div></div><div style=\"margin:0.65em 0;padding:0.55em 0.7em;border-left:3px solid #a335ee;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.04);border-radius:0 4px 4px 0\"><p><strong style=\"color:#1eff00\">Spread Ammo</strong></p><p>Instead of making an attack roll, you fire a 15-foot cone. Each creature in the cone must make a Dexterity saving throw against your Ammo DC. On a failed save, a creature takes [[/r 1d10]] Piercing damage.</p><div style=\"margin:0.45em 0 0.1em 0.35em;padding:0.4em 0.55em;border-left:2px solid #a335ee;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border-radius:0 3px 3px 0\"><p>▸ Upgrade — <strong style=\"color:#a335ee\">Spread Ammo Upgrade</strong></p><p>Your Spread Ammo now deals an extra [[/r 1d6]] Piercing damage.</p></div></div><div style=\"margin:0.65em 0;padding:0.55em 0.7em;border-left:3px solid #a335ee;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.04);border-radius:0 4px 4px 0\"><p><strong style=\"color:#1eff00\">Cluster Ammo</strong></p><p>This ammo deals no weapon damage. On a hit, it explodes, dealing [[/r 2d6]] Fire damage to the target and each creature within 5 feet of it.</p><div style=\"margin:0.45em 0 0.1em 0.35em;padding:0.4em 0.55em;border-left:2px solid #a335ee;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border-radius:0 3px 3px 0\"><p>▸ Upgrade — <strong style=\"color:#a335ee\">Cluster Ammo Upgrade</strong></p><p>Your Cluster Ammo explosion now deals [[/r 3d6]] Fire damage.</p></div></div><div style=\"margin:0.65em 0;padding:0.55em 0.7em;border-left:3px solid #a335ee;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.04);border-radius:0 4px 4px 0\"><p><strong style=\"color:#1eff00\">Recover Ammo</strong></p><p>Instead of taking damage, a willing creature hit by this ammo regains [[/r 1d4]] hit points.</p><div style=\"margin:0.45em 0 0.1em 0.35em;padding:0.4em 0.55em;border-left:2px solid #a335ee;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border-radius:0 3px 3px 0\"><p>▸ Upgrade — <strong style=\"color:#a335ee\">Recover Ammo Upgrade</strong></p><p>Your Recover Ammo now restores [[/r 2d4]] + your Proficiency Bonus hit points.</p></div></div><div style=\"margin:0.65em 0;padding:0.55em 0.7em;border-left:3px solid #0070dd;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.04);border-radius:0 4px 4px 0\"><p><strong style=\"color:#0070dd\">Poison Ammo</strong></p><p>A creature hit by this ammo must succeed on a Constitution saving throw against your Ammo DC or have the Poisoned condition for 1 minute. The creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on a success.</p></div><div style=\"margin:0.65em 0;padding:0.55em 0.7em;border-left:3px solid #0070dd;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.04);border-radius:0 4px 4px 0\"><p><strong style=\"color:#0070dd\">Paralysis Ammo</strong></p><p>A creature hit by this ammo must succeed on a Constitution saving throw against your Ammo DC or become Incapacitated and have its Speed reduced to 0 until the end of your next turn. If it fails the save by 5 or more, it is Paralyzed instead until the end of your next turn.</p></div><div style=\"margin:0.65em 0;padding:0.55em 0.7em;border-left:3px solid #0070dd;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.04);border-radius:0 4px 4px 0\"><p><strong style=\"color:#0070dd\">Sticky Ammo</strong></p><p>A creature hit by this ammo must succeed on a Strength saving throw against your Ammo DC or have the Restrained condition for 1 minute. The creature can use its action to attempt to escape (escape DC equal to your Ammo DC).</p></div><div style=\"margin:0.65em 0;padding:0.55em 0.7em;border-left:3px solid #0070dd;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.04);border-radius:0 4px 4px 0\"><p><strong style=\"color:#0070dd\">Slicing Ammo</strong></p><p>Instead of making a ranged weapon attack, choose a target within this weapon's long range. The target must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw against your Ammo DC, taking [[/r 4d6]] Slashing damage on a failed save, or half as much on a successful one. If the target is beyond this weapon's normal range, it has advantage on the save.</p></div><div style=\"margin:0.65em 0;padding:0.55em 0.7em;border-left:3px solid #0070dd;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.04);border-radius:0 4px 4px 0\"><p><strong style=\"color:#0070dd\">Wyvern Ammo</strong></p><p>You do not make an attack roll with this ammo. Instead, each creature in a 15-foot cone must make a Dexterity saving throw against your Ammo DC, taking [[/r 2d12]] Fire damage on a failed save, or half as much on a successful one.</p></div>",
      "chat": "<p>Requires Attunement</p><p>Ammo DC = 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Dexterity modifier</p><hr><div style=\"margin:0.4em 0;padding:0.35em 0.55em;border-left:3px solid #c0c0c0;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.04);border-radius:0 4px 4px 0\"><p><strong style=\"color:#c0c0c0\">Mastery (Slow)</strong></p></div><div style=\"margin:0.4em 0;padding:0.35em 0.55em;border-left:3px solid #ff8000;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.04);border-radius:0 4px 4px 0\"><p><strong style=\"color:#c0c0c0\">Magazine</strong></p><p style=\"margin:0.2em 0 0 0.35em\">▸ <strong style=\"color:#1eff00\">Magazine Upgrade I</strong></p><p style=\"margin:0.2em 0 0 0.35em\">▸ <strong style=\"color:#0070dd\">Magazine Upgrade II</strong></p><p style=\"margin:0.2em 0 0 0.35em\">▸ <strong style=\"color:#a335ee\">Magazine Upgrade III</strong></p><p style=\"margin:0.2em 0 0 0.35em\">▸ <strong style=\"color:#ff8000\">Magazine Upgrade IV</strong></p></div><div style=\"margin:0.4em 0;padding:0.35em 0.55em;border-left:3px solid #c0c0c0;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.04);border-radius:0 4px 4px 0\"><p><strong style=\"color:#c0c0c0\">Reload</strong></p><p><strong>Action.</strong></p></div><div style=\"margin:0.4em 0;padding:0.35em 0.55em;border-left:3px solid #1eff00;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.04);border-radius:0 4px 4px 0\"><p><strong style=\"color:#1eff00\">Ignition</strong></p></div><div style=\"margin:0.4em 0;padding:0.35em 0.55em;border-left:3px solid #a335ee;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.04);border-radius:0 4px 4px 0\"><p><strong style=\"color:#1eff00\">Wyvernheart</strong></p><p><strong>Bonus Action.</strong></p><p style=\"margin:0.2em 0 0 0.35em\">▸ <strong style=\"color:#0070dd\">Wyvernheart Upgrade I</strong></p><p style=\"margin:0.2em 0 0 0.35em\">▸ <strong style=\"color:#a335ee\">Wyvernheart Upgrade II</strong></p></div><div style=\"margin:0.4em 0;padding:0.35em 0.55em;border-left:3px solid #0070dd;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.04);border-radius:0 4px 4px 0\"><p><strong style=\"color:#1eff00\">Guard</strong></p><p><strong>Reaction.</strong></p><p style=\"margin:0.2em 0 0 0.35em\">▸ <strong style=\"color:#0070dd\">Guard Upgrade I</strong></p></div><div style=\"margin:0.4em 0;padding:0.35em 0.55em;border-left:3px solid #ff8000;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.04);border-radius:0 4px 4px 0\"><p><strong style=\"color:#1eff00\">Special Ammo</strong></p><p style=\"margin:0.2em 0 0 0.35em\">▸ <strong style=\"color:#0070dd\">Special Ammo Upgrade I</strong></p><p style=\"margin:0.2em 0 0 0.35em\">▸ <strong style=\"color:#a335ee\">Special Ammo Upgrade II</strong></p><p style=\"margin:0.2em 0 0 0.35em\">▸ <strong style=\"color:#ff8000\">Special Ammo Upgrade III</strong></p></div><div style=\"margin:0.4em 0;padding:0.35em 0.55em;border-left:3px solid #0070dd;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.04);border-radius:0 4px 4px 0\"><p><strong style=\"color:#0070dd\">Wyverncounter</strong></p></div><div style=\"margin:0.4em 0;padding:0.35em 0.55em;border-left:3px solid #ff8000;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.04);border-radius:0 4px 4px 0\"><p><strong style=\"color:#a335ee\">Wyvernpiercer</strong></p><p><strong>Action.</strong></p><p style=\"margin:0.2em 0 0 0.35em\">▸ <strong style=\"color:#ff8000\">Wyvernpiercer Upgrade</strong></p></div><div style=\"margin:0.4em 0;padding:0.35em 0.55em;border-left:3px solid #ff8000;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.04);border-radius:0 4px 4px 0\"><p><strong style=\"color:#ff8000\">Ignition Mode</strong></p><p><strong>Bonus Action.</strong></p></div>"
    },
